course: dictionary
lesson: 14908
title: Recyclable
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Put the empty glass jar in the recycling bin, because glass is recyclable.» The word is made of three parts: re- means again, cycle means a loop or round, and -able means can be. So recyclable means able to go round again.
explain: When something is recyclable, it is collected and made into new things instead of being thrown away. «Old metal cans can be melted down and made into new cans.» The cans are not wasted; they go round again.
explain: Ask yourself: can this be recycled? «Ella checked the label on the box to see if the packaging was recyclable.» The label, or the recycling symbol, helps her decide. Recyclable is an adjective, and recyclables is a noun for the things that can be recycled.
fact: Recyclable means able to be recycled: collected and made into new things instead of being thrown away.
fact: Paper, cardboard, glass, metal cans and many plastics are recyclable.
fact: «Recyclables» means things that can be recycled, such as bottles and cans.
fact: Food waste cannot be recycled in the same way, but it can be composted instead.
fact: Look for the recycling symbol on packaging to help you check if it is recyclable.
exercise: «Put the empty glass jar in the recycling bin, because glass is recyclable.» What does recyclable mean? | Able to be eaten | *Able to be recycled and made into new things | Very old and broken | Able to be thrown away in the rubbish
exercise: Ella says recyclable is just a fancy word for «can be thrown away». Why is she wrong? | *Recyclable things are collected and made into new things, not thrown away | Recyclable means very old | Recyclable means the same as rubbish | Recyclable means heavy and hard to lift
exercise: «Paper and cardboard are recyclable, so put them in the blue bin.» Find and copy one word that means able to be recycled. | bin | paper | blue | *recyclable
test: «The cereal box is made of cardboard, which is recyclable.» In this sentence, what does recyclable mean? | Dirty and wet | Made of wood | *Able to be recycled and made into something new | Too big to carry
test: Which symbol on packaging helps you check if something is recyclable? | A star | A question mark | *The recycling symbol | A smiling face
exam: Which item is recyclable? | Half-eaten sandwich | Banana peel | *Clean cardboard box | Wet tissue
